Historical fix: 1bd2dbc — "bugfix for append not set self.len properly (#347)"

Applying this patch installs the *buggy* pre-fix code: `SmallVec::append`
copies the source buffer into the destination but never updates
`self.len()` to the combined total, leaving `len == old_self_len`.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -1275,7 +1275,6 @@ impl<T, const N: usize> SmallVec<T, N> {
         // SAFETY: we have a mutable reference to each vector and each uniquely owns its memory.
         // so the ranges can't overlap
         unsafe { copy_nonoverlapping(other.as_ptr(), ptr, other_len) };
-        unsafe { self.set_len(total_len) }
     }

     #[inline]
